<!--charlatan-->
[
The Great Charlatan was a native Askavan cultist living in the Third Century, during the tail-end what historians of Askava refer to as the "First Colony Era".
<br>
(link: "And...")[{The Charlatan's cult turned many Nurandahid magi in Apesai and Navveh into apostates, practicioners of false and dark superstitions.
<br>
(link: "And...")[In the ensuing conflict, the cultists failed to secede from the empire, their leader was killed, and in a last, savage bid to win the war, the remaining apostates detonated a terrible magic upon the Navveh Crossing - the sole land route from the Nurandah heartlands into Askava, now no more.
<br>
(link: "And finally...")[The resulting earthquake buried the old city of Navveh, closed the western gap in the Besarag, and plunged Askava into a dark age.
<br>
The region was not contacted again until the re-establishment of the Second Colony in Apesai, the sea being the only remaining way to access continental Askava.
<br>
So yes, you know the //Great Charlatan//.
]]}]
<br>
["Yeah, //that// Charlatan,"]<VehVehLine| she says eagerly, too eager for the subject matter. ["I'm interested their magic."]<VehVehLine|
<br>
You don't like where this is going.
<br>
($funcInnerConvo: (dm:
	"<!--A-->\"I see... So are you some sort of historian?\"", "history",
	"<!--B-->\"Umm... interested - from a ethical perspective? Like, human rights and magical abuses?\"", "ethical",
	"<!--C-->\"Let me guess, anthropology! You're studying the various superstitions of malificers!\"", "anthropology",
	"<!--D-->\"What //magic// could a nativist ideologue possibly have? Is this a round-about way to say you're a political scientist? \"", "polisci",
	"<!--E-->\"...\"", "magicBrainwash",
	
))
<br>
